Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:

> impression supported that these two terms (lock-pick, skeleton key)
> are quite synonymous[*], especially given their universal usage (they
> work on _every_ door, chest, box) in nethack.

They are not exactly synonyms, even though they both open many different
locks.
A skeleton key is a janitor's key made for legal use to open a certain set
of locks.
A lock-pick is a burglar's tool, not necessarily for any specific locks,
just for as many locks as possible.

